<section class="cxx entity method">

  <h1 id="Arcadia_ByteArray_isContiguous">Arcadia_ByteArray_isContiguous</h1>

  <my-signature><code>
  Arcadia_BooleanValue<br>
  Arcadia_ByteArray_isContiguous<br>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;(<br>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Arcadia_Thread* thread<br>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Arcadia_ByteArray const* self<br>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;)
  </code></my-signature>

  <my-summary>Determines whether the byte array stores its logical bytes in one contiguous range.</my-summary>

  <section class="cxx parameters">
    <h1>Parameters</h1>
    <div>
      <div><code>Arcadia_Thread* thread</code></div>
      <div>A pointer to the calling thread.</div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div><code>Arcadia_ByteArray const* self</code></div>
      <div>A pointer to this byte array.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cxx return-value">
    <h1>Return value</h1>
    <p><code>Arcadia_BooleanValue_True</code> if this instance provides contiguous storage; <code>Arcadia_BooleanValue_False</code> otherwise.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="cxx remarks">
    <h1>Remarks</h1>
    <p>The result is stable throughout this instance's lifetime. Contiguity does not imply mutability, resizability, ownership of memory, or pointer stability across resizing. Native pointer borrowing still requires that the owner remain reachable.</p>
  </section>

</section>
